{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 27, :comments ["Elohim you shall not curse, nor shall you curse a prince among your people — Scripture speaks of the normal situation: because kings and judges adjudicate monetary and capital cases, people are accustomed to curse them. So too it says: ״גם במדעך מלך אל תקלל״. And so too it says: ״כי קללת אלהים תלוי״ — when people see a man hanging they curse the judges; therefore He commanded: do not let his corpse remain overnight."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:41.328993173Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}